  "title": "Erdős Problem #521",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $(\\epsilon_k)_{k\\geq 0}$ be independently uniformly chosen at random from $\\{-1,1\\}$. If $R_n$ counts the number of real roots of $f_n(z)=\\sum_{0\\leq k\\leq n}\\epsilon_k z^k$ then is it true that, almost surely, $ \\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{R_n}{\\log n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi}? $ ",
